  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a nurse. A patient's daughter phones asking how her mother is. The mother is stable but has had a difficult night. The daughter lives four hours away and is asking whether she should travel today. How do you handle the call?$qb$, $qb$Describe what has actually happened and let her decide about travelling$qb$, $qb$Say her mother is stable and that visiting is a decision for the family$qb$, $qb$Say her mother is stable and that there is no need to travel today$qb$, $qb$Suggest she speaks to the doctor, who can advise about travelling$qb$, $qb$Say everything is fine so that she is not worried unnecessarily$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a small team. One member has been told by a customer that a delivery will be late, but has not passed this on. You find out from the customer three days later. How do you raise it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they did with the information when they received it$qb$, $qb$Explain the effect the delay had and ask them to pass such news on$qb$, $qb$Tell them clearly that news like this must always be passed on$qb$, $qb$Set up a rule that all customer calls are logged in future$qb$, $qb$Let it go, since the customer told you in the end anyway$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a bank counter. A customer is asking loudly about a charge on his account, and other customers are waiting and listening. The charge appears to be correct. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Offer to go through it with him away from the counter$qb$, $qb$Explain the charge calmly and clearly where you are$qb$, $qb$Ask him to lower his voice so you can help him properly$qb$, $qb$Reverse the charge to end the situation quickly$qb$, $qb$Tell him the charge is correct and call the next customer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
