  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a shop assistant. A customer has asked for a refund on an item bought six weeks ago. Your shop's policy allows refunds within four weeks, and you cannot make exceptions. How do you tell her?$qb$, $qb$Tell her plainly that six weeks is outside the policy, and say what you can offer$qb$, $qb$Explain the four week policy and apologise that you cannot help$qb$, $qb$Explain that you personally would help but the policy prevents it$qb$, $qb$Suggest she writes to head office, who may make an exception$qb$, $qb$Tell her the policy is four weeks and leave it at that$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a teacher. A parent has emailed twice asking about their child's progress. You have been busy and have not replied. The parent's second email is noticeably shorter and colder. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Reply today with the information, and apologise for the two week silence$qb$, $qb$Reply today with the information asked for, without raising the delay$qb$, $qb$Reply today apologising, and say when the full information will follow$qb$, $qb$Invite the parent in for a meeting rather than replying by email$qb$, $qb$Reply when you have the full picture of the child's progress$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a call centre. A caller is describing a problem and you realise the fault is with a different company's product, not yours. The caller sounds tired and has clearly been passed around already. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell him it is not our product, and give him the name of who to call$qb$, $qb$Explain that this is another company's product and he needs to contact them$qb$, $qb$Ask more about the problem before deciding whose product it is$qb$, $qb$Try to help him with the problem even though it is not ours$qb$, $qb$Transfer him to another department who may be able to help$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are an engineer. A customer has asked you to explain why a repair will cost as much as it does. The reason involves technical detail she is unlikely to follow. How do you answer?$qb$, $qb$Explain what has to be replaced and why that part is expensive$qb$, $qb$Explain the technical fault in full so she has the whole picture$qb$, $qb$Tell her the cost reflects the parts and the labour involved$qb$, $qb$Offer to show her the faulty part so she can see for herself$qb$, $qb$Tell her it is a standard charge for this kind of repair$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a team of six. You have decided to change how work is allocated. Two people will clearly gain from the change and two will clearly lose. How do you announce it?$qb$, $qb$Speak to the two who lose out first, then tell the whole team together$qb$, $qb$Tell the whole team together and explain the reasoning behind it$qb$, $qb$Speak to all six individually before it becomes general knowledge$qb$, $qb$Send it in writing so everyone receives the same wording$qb$, $qb$Tell the two who gain first, since they will support it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a receptionist at a clinic. A patient has been waiting fifty minutes past his appointment time. The doctor is running late and you do not know by how much. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell him the doctor is running late, find out how long, and come back to him$qb$, $qb$Apologise for the wait and tell him the doctor is running late$qb$, $qb$Apologise and ask him to bear with you a little longer$qb$, $qb$Tell him the doctor will see him as soon as possible$qb$, $qb$Say nothing unless he asks, since he can see the waiting room$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a site manager. A delivery driver has arrived with the wrong materials. He speaks little English and you speak none of his language. The load must be sorted out today. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Show him the order and the load side by side so the difference is visible$qb$, $qb$Speak slowly and clearly to explain what has been delivered wrongly$qb$, $qb$Phone his depot and explain the problem to someone there$qb$, $qb$Use a translation app to explain the problem to him$qb$, $qb$Refuse the delivery and let his company work out what went wrong$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a small office. An email you sent about a policy change has been forwarded around and people are reading it as a criticism of one team. That was not your intention. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Write again saying plainly what you did and did not mean$qb$, $qb$Speak to the team that feels criticised and explain your intention$qb$, $qb$Ask people to stop forwarding the email around the office$qb$, $qb$Wait for it to settle, since explaining may draw more attention$qb$, $qb$Point out that the email says nothing about that team$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COM-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a mechanic. A customer left her car for a service. You have found a further fault that will cost more than the service itself, and she has not authorised the extra work. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Phone her now, describe the fault and the cost, and ask what she wants$qb$, $qb$Phone her to say there is a further fault and ask her to call back$qb$, $qb$Complete the service and tell her about the fault when she collects$qb$, $qb$Do the extra work as well, since the car clearly needs it$qb$, $qb$Note the fault on the invoice and leave her to read it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
