  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two colleagues disagree about how a job should be done. Both approaches would work. You have to decide. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$That both understand why the choice was made$qb$, $qb$That the decision is made quickly$qb$, $qb$That the more experienced person's view carries weight$qb$, $qb$That each gets their way on alternate occasions$qb$, $qb$That the decision is recorded in writing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone accuses you in a meeting of something you did not do. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they are referring to specifically$qb$, $qb$Deny it clearly and move the meeting on$qb$, $qb$Say you will discuss it with them afterwards$qb$, $qb$Explain in detail why the accusation is wrong$qb$, $qb$Say nothing and raise it with your manager later$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A disagreement between two team members has been going on for weeks. Each says the other started it. What is the most useful thing to establish?$qb$, $qb$What each of them needs in order to work together now$qb$, $qb$What actually happened at the start of the disagreement$qb$, $qb$Which of the two accounts is more accurate$qb$, $qb$Whether either of them wants to move teams$qb$, $qb$How much the disagreement is costing in lost work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An angry customer says something that is factually wrong about what your company did. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Deal with the complaint first and correct the fact once he is calmer$qb$, $qb$Correct the fact straight away so the discussion is accurate$qb$, $qb$Let the error stand, since arguing will make things worse$qb$, $qb$Ask him where he got that information from$qb$, $qb$Explain the full sequence of what actually happened$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two departments are blaming each other for a delay that is still holding up the work. Neither has refused to deal with the other. You need it fixed. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Get both in a room and work forward from where things stand now$qb$, $qb$Establish which department caused the delay$qb$, $qb$Ask each department separately what went wrong$qb$, $qb$Escalate it to the heads of both departments$qb$, $qb$Fix it yourself and let them settle the blame later$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague raises their voice at you in front of others. What is the best immediate response?$qb$, $qb$Suggest continuing the conversation somewhere else$qb$, $qb$Answer the point they are making calmly$qb$, $qb$Tell them you will not be spoken to like that$qb$, $qb$Walk away and let them cool down$qb$, $qb$Raise your own voice so they know it is not acceptable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have to give a decision that one person will strongly dislike. What reduces the conflict most?$qb$, $qb$Telling them before it becomes general knowledge$qb$, $qb$Explaining the reasoning behind the decision$qb$, $qb$Giving them a chance to respond to it$qb$, $qb$Delivering it in writing so it is clear$qb$, $qb$Softening the wording so it lands more gently$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two people are arguing and each keeps repeating the same point. What does this usually mean?$qb$, $qb$Neither feels the other has taken their point in$qb$, $qb$Neither is willing to change their position$qb$, $qb$The argument has run out of new information$qb$, $qb$Both are more interested in winning than resolving$qb$, $qb$Someone else needs to make the decision$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A supplier is angry about a late payment that was your company's error. What should you do first?$qb$, $qb$Confirm the error and tell him when he will be paid$qb$, $qb$Apologise for the delay and promise to look into it$qb$, $qb$Explain how the error happened in your accounts team$qb$, $qb$Ask him to send the invoice again so you can check$qb$, $qb$Tell him it is being dealt with by another department$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are mediating between two colleagues. One argues far more fluently than the other. What is the main risk to guard against?$qb$, $qb$The better argued case being taken as the stronger one$qb$, $qb$The quieter person giving way just to end the discussion$qb$, $qb$The discussion drifting away from the actual disagreement$qb$, $qb$One of them interrupting the other repeatedly$qb$, $qb$The meeting running longer than the time you have$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone sends you an angry email late at night. What is usually the best response?$qb$, $qb$Reply in the morning to the substance of it$qb$, $qb$Reply straight away so it is not left hanging$qb$, $qb$Speak to them in person the next day instead$qb$, $qb$Forward it to your manager for advice$qb$, $qb$Reply saying you found the tone unacceptable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A conflict between two staff has been settled, but one of them clearly still feels aggrieved. What is the best step?$qb$, $qb$Ask them what would need to change for it to feel settled$qb$, $qb$Give it time, since feelings take longer than agreements$qb$, $qb$Remind them that the matter has been resolved$qb$, $qb$Watch to see whether it affects their work$qb$, $qb$Ask the other person whether they have noticed it too$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You realise partway through a disagreement that you are in the wrong. What is the best action?$qb$, $qb$Say so straight away and change your position$qb$, $qb$Finish making your point and reconsider afterwards$qb$, $qb$Move the conversation towards a compromise$qb$, $qb$Ask for time to think it over$qb$, $qb$Let the argument end without conceding directly$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two customers in your shop are arguing loudly with each other. What is the best first action?$qb$, $qb$Speak to each of them separately to break the exchange$qb$, $qb$Ask them both to lower their voices$qb$, $qb$Ask them both to leave the shop$qb$, $qb$Stand nearby so they know they are being watched$qb$, $qb$Continue serving and let them sort it out$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member complains to you about another team member. What should you do first?$qb$, $qb$Ask whether they have raised it with the person themselves$qb$, $qb$Listen fully and then speak to the other person$qb$, $qb$Offer to sit down with both of them together$qb$, $qb$Ask others whether they have noticed the same thing$qb$, $qb$Tell them to raise it directly and not with you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A disagreement in your team is really about workload, but it is being argued about as a difference over method. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Name the workload issue and deal with that instead$qb$, $qb$Settle the method question and see if the tension eases$qb$, $qb$Ask both people what they think the argument is about$qb$, $qb$Deal with the method now and workload separately later$qb$, $qb$Let them settle the method between themselves$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone has apologised to you but you do not think they understand what upset you. What is the most useful response?$qb$, $qb$Accept it and say plainly what the difficulty was$qb$, $qb$Accept it and leave the explanation for another time$qb$, $qb$Ask them what they think they are apologising for$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since pressing further may seem ungracious$qb$, $qb$Decline it until they show they have understood$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a restaurant. A customer is complaining loudly that his meal took an hour. He is right, and the kitchen was short-staffed. Other diners are watching. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Go to his table, agree the wait was too long, and say what you will do about it$qb$, $qb$Send a member of staff over to apologise to him for the long wait$qb$, $qb$Ask him to step aside so the other diners are not disturbed$qb$, $qb$Explain that the kitchen was short-staffed this evening$qb$, $qb$Offer him a free meal so that the complaint stops$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a team of eight. Two members had a disagreement in a meeting yesterday, and the rest of the team saw it. Today they are both being professional but cold. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Speak to each separately, then decide whether they need to meet$qb$, $qb$Bring them together today to clear the air properly$qb$, $qb$Speak to the team about how disagreements are handled$qb$, $qb$Leave it alone, since both are behaving professionally$qb$, $qb$Tell them both that yesterday must not happen again$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work on a hospital reception desk. A man is demanding to see a doctor now. His appointment is in an hour and the doctors are all with patients. He is becoming louder. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell him plainly what you can do and by when, and stay with him while he decides$qb$, $qb$Explain that his appointment is in an hour and the doctors are busy$qb$, $qb$Ask him to take a seat and wait for his appointment time$qb$, $qb$Tell him that shouting will not get him seen any sooner$qb$, $qb$Call security, since he is disturbing the waiting room$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a warehouse. Two members of your team have had an argument about a mistake. One made the mistake; the other pointed it out in front of everyone. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Speak to both about how mistakes get raised here, and to each about their part$qb$, $qb$Speak to the one who raised it publicly about how to do it privately$qb$, $qb$Speak to the one who made the mistake about what went wrong$qb$, $qb$Bring them together and ask them to sort it out between themselves$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since a mistake was made and it needed pointing out$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a landlord's agent. A tenant is angry about a repair that has taken three weeks. The delay was caused by a contractor who did not turn up twice. How do you handle the call?$qb$, $qb$Agree the delay is unacceptable, and give her a date you will hold to$qb$, $qb$Apologise for the delay and explain what the contractor did$qb$, $qb$Tell her you will chase the contractor again today$qb$, $qb$Explain that contractor delays are outside your control$qb$, $qb$Tell her the repair is booked and she will hear in due course$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a teacher. Two students have fallen out and the rest of the class has taken sides. The lesson is being disrupted. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Settle the lesson first, then speak to the two of them afterwards$qb$, $qb$Speak to the two students outside the room now$qb$, $qb$Separate the two students and continue the lesson$qb$, $qb$Tell the class that the argument is not their business$qb$, $qb$Ask the two students what the disagreement is about$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a small office. A member of staff has come to you upset about a comment a colleague made. The colleague says it was a joke. Both accounts of the words are the same. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Deal with the effect it had, regardless of how it was meant$qb$, $qb$Explain to the person upset that no offence was intended$qb$, $qb$Ask the colleague to apologise for the way it landed$qb$, $qb$Tell both to be more careful about how they speak to each other$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since both agree it was meant as a joke$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a garage. A customer is disputing a bill, saying he was quoted less. Your written quote matches the bill, but he says he was told a lower figure on the phone. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show him the written quote and ask what he was told on the phone$qb$, $qb$Check with whoever took his call before you say anything to him$qb$, $qb$Show him the written quote and hold to the figure on the bill$qb$, $qb$Reduce the bill to the figure he says he was quoted$qb$, $qb$Tell him the written quote is what counts and the bill stands$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a project. Two senior people on it disagree about the approach and each has been lobbying you separately. The project is stalling. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Get them both in one room and put the choice in front of them together$qb$, $qb$Decide between the two approaches yourself and announce it$qb$, $qb$Ask each of them to put their case in writing$qb$, $qb$Take it to the sponsor and ask them to settle it$qb$, $qb$Keep talking to each separately until one of them gives way$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a call centre. A caller is being personally abusive about you rather than about the problem. Your company policy allows you to end such calls. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell him what you can help with, and that you will end the call if it continues$qb$, $qb$Ask him to keep to the problem itself so that you can help him$qb$, $qb$Ignore the personal remarks and keep working on the problem$qb$, $qb$End the call now, since the policy allows it$qb$, $qb$Tell him you find his behaviour unacceptable and unnecessary$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a shift leader. A member of your team has complained that another regularly leaves the worst jobs for the next shift. You have looked and the complaint appears to be justified. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Speak to the person about the pattern, using what you have seen yourself$qb$, $qb$Speak to the person about the complaint that has been made$qb$, $qb$Change how the jobs are allocated so it cannot happen$qb$, $qb$Bring both of them together to discuss the allocation$qb$, $qb$Tell the complainant to raise it with the person directly$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a shop. Two of your staff want the same week off in the summer and both have asked first. Only one can be spared. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Explain the constraint to both and ask them to propose a split$qb$, $qb$Decide between them and explain the reasoning to both$qb$, $qb$Give it to whoever asked first and tell the other why$qb$, $qb$Ask them to sort it out between themselves$qb$, $qb$Refuse both requests so that neither is favoured$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a community worker. Two neighbours are in a long-running dispute about noise and both have asked you to intervene. Each wants you to tell the other to stop. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Ask each what they could live with, rather than what they want stopped$qb$, $qb$Meet them both together and hear each account$qb$, $qb$Set out what the rules on noise actually say$qb$, $qb$Tell each of them what the other has said$qb$, $qb$Tell them this is a matter for them to resolve privately$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CRD-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a supervisor. During a disagreement about a rota, a team member says something you find personally insulting, then immediately says he did not mean it. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Finish the rota discussion, then deal with the remark separately$qb$, $qb$Stop and tell him now that the remark was not acceptable$qb$, $qb$Accept that he did not mean it and carry on with the rota$qb$, $qb$Say nothing now and raise it with him at his next review$qb$, $qb$Let it go entirely, since he withdrew it straight away$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-001$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Knowing what you will do if there is no agreement tells you when to walk ______.$qb$, $qb$away$qb$, $qb$back$qb$, $qb$slowly$qb$, $qb$together$qb$, $qb$again$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-002$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A price is easier to hold when you can say what the buyer gets for ______.$qb$, $qb$it$qb$, $qb$less$qb$, $qb$free$qb$, $qb$waiting$qb$, $qb$asking$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-004$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Opening with your lowest acceptable figure leaves you nothing to ______.$qb$, $qb$concede$qb$, $qb$measure$qb$, $qb$explain$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$compare$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-005$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A concession given without asking for anything back teaches the other side to keep ______.$qb$, $qb$pushing$qb$, $qb$waiting$qb$, $qb$talking$qb$, $qb$agreeing$qb$, $qb$returning$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$When a negotiation is stuck on price, adding delivery time or payment terms gives both sides something to ______.$qb$, $qb$trade$qb$, $qb$ignore$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, $qb$count$qb$, $qb$approve$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Agreeing the easy items first shows both sides that agreement is ______.$qb$, $qb$possible$qb$, $qb$printed$qb$, $qb$cheap$qb$, $qb$required$qb$, $qb$temporary$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A deadline set by the other side is worth testing before treating it as ______.$qb$, $qb$fixed$qb$, $qb$fair$qb$, $qb$urgent$qb$, $qb$public$qb$, $qb$recent$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Writing down what was agreed prevents each side remembering a different ______.$qb$, $qb$version$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$price$qb$, $qb$person$qb$, $qb$reason$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Saying no to a bad deal protects the value of your next ______.$qb$, $qb$yes$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$customer$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$invoice$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Naming your reason for a figure makes it harder to treat as an opening ______.$qb$, $qb$bid$qb$, $qb$reason$qb$, $qb$discount$qb$, $qb$question$qb$, $qb$favour$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The side that speaks first about money sets the range the talk happens ______.$qb$, $qb$within$qb$, $qb$after$qb$, $qb$before$qb$, $qb$against$qb$, $qb$beyond$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$An agreement that leaves one side feeling cheated tends not to ______.$qb$, $qb$last$qb$, $qb$close$qb$, $qb$matter$qb$, $qb$spread$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Asking for time to think is cheaper than agreeing to something you have not ______.$qb$, $qb$costed$qb$, $qb$signed$qb$, $qb$offered$qb$, $qb$printed$qb$, $qb$filed$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$When both sides want the same thing, the disagreement is usually about ______.$qb$, $qb$terms$qb$, $qb$people$qb$, $qb$history$qb$, $qb$location$qb$, $qb$past$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A request backed by what it saves the other side is stronger than one backed by what you ______.$qb$, $qb$need$qb$, $qb$paid$qb$, $qb$dismiss$qb$, $qb$lose$qb$, $qb$lack$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You ask for 100 rupees and the buyer offers 50. He suggests splitting the difference at 75. What is worth noticing?$qb$, $qb$Where the split lands depends entirely on where he opened$qb$, $qb$Seventy five may still be above what you would have accepted$qb$, $qb$Splitting the difference ends the discussion quickly$qb$, $qb$He has moved as far as you have from his opening$qb$, $qb$Seventy five is fair because both sides moved equally$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are buying from a supplier and want a lower price. What is most likely to get you one?$qb$, $qb$Showing what you would order at the lower price$qb$, $qb$Telling them a competitor charges less$qb$, $qb$Asking them directly for their best price$qb$, $qb$Explaining that your budget will not stretch further$qb$, $qb$Saying you will go elsewhere unless they move$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer asks for a discount you cannot give. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Offer something else of value instead of money off$qb$, $qb$Explain why the price is what it is$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make the price work for them$qb$, $qb$Hold the price and let them decide$qb$, $qb$Give a smaller discount than they asked for$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Before a negotiation, what is the single most useful thing to work out?$qb$, $qb$What you will do if there is no agreement$qb$, $qb$What the other side is likely to open with$qb$, $qb$What your ideal outcome would look like$qb$, $qb$How much time you have to reach agreement$qb$, $qb$Who has more to lose from no agreement$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The other side opens with a figure far below what you expected. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Ask how they arrived at it$qb$, $qb$Counter with a figure equally far the other way$qb$, $qb$Say the figure is not workable and give yours$qb$, $qb$Ignore it and restate what you want$qb$, $qb$End the discussion, since the gap is too wide$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have agreed most terms but one point remains and both sides are stuck. What is most likely to move it?$qb$, $qb$Finding out why that point matters to them$qb$, $qb$Offering to split the difference on it$qb$, $qb$Reminding them how much is already agreed$qb$, $qb$Asking them to make the next move$qb$, $qb$Setting a deadline to force a decision$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A supplier says the price is fixed and cannot change. What should you test first?$qb$, $qb$Whether anything other than price can move$qb$, $qb$Whether the price is fixed for all customers$qb$, $qb$Whether a larger order would change it$qb$, $qb$Whether another supplier would charge less$qb$, $qb$Whether they will hold the price if you wait$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are negotiating and realise you have more to lose than the other side if there is no agreement. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Work on making no agreement less costly for you$qb$, $qb$Avoid letting them see how much you need it$qb$, $qb$Move faster to reach agreement before they notice$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make agreement attractive to them$qb$, $qb$Accept the best terms available now$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team leader asks you to take on extra work. You are willing but stretched. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Say what you would have to drop to take it on$qb$, $qb$Ask how urgent it is before agreeing$qb$, $qb$Agree, and mention that you are stretched$qb$, $qb$Say you can do it if nobody else can$qb$, $qb$Agree now and raise the workload later$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have made three concessions and received none. What should you do next?$qb$, $qb$Ask for something in return before conceding again$qb$, $qb$Point out that the movement has been one way$qb$, $qb$Make no further concessions and wait$qb$, $qb$Make a smaller concession to keep things moving$qb$, $qb$Withdraw one of the concessions already made$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two people want the last available meeting slot with an important client. What is the most useful question to ask?$qb$, $qb$What each of them needs the meeting for$qb$, $qb$Which of them asked for the slot first$qb$, $qb$Which meeting is more valuable to the business$qb$, $qb$Whether either could meet the client another day$qb$, $qb$Whether both could attend the same meeting$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A negotiation has gone quiet and the other side has not replied for a week. What is the best step?$qb$, $qb$Contact them with something new to consider$qb$, $qb$Contact them asking whether they are still interested$qb$, $qb$Wait, since chasing may weaken your position$qb$, $qb$Withdraw the offer to prompt a response$qb$, $qb$Assume it is over and look elsewhere$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are agreeing a deadline with a client. They want it sooner than you can manage. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they need by that date, since part may be enough$qb$, $qb$Explain what makes the earlier date impossible$qb$, $qb$Offer the earliest date you can genuinely meet$qb$, $qb$Agree the date and warn them it may slip$qb$, $qb$Agree the date and work out how later$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually makes an agreement hold up over time?$qb$, $qb$Both sides understanding what they gained$qb$, $qb$The agreement being written down clearly$qb$, $qb$Both sides having conceded roughly equally$qb$, $qb$The agreement being reached quickly$qb$, $qb$A senior person having approved it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer says another supplier has quoted twenty per cent less. What should you find out first?$qb$, $qb$What the other quote actually covers$qb$, $qb$Whether the customer wants you to match it$qb$, $qb$Which supplier gave the quote$qb$, $qb$How firm the other quote is$qb$, $qb$Whether you could match the figure$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are negotiating on behalf of your team and reach a point beyond your authority. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Say you need to check, and agree when you will come back$qb$, $qb$Say the point is beyond what you can agree today$qb$, $qb$Agree in principle and confirm afterwards$qb$, $qb$Ask them to lower the request to something you can agree$qb$, $qb$Agree it, since your manager would probably accept$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The other side keeps returning to a point you have already settled. What does this usually mean?$qb$, $qb$The point is not actually settled for them$qb$, $qb$They are testing whether you will move again$qb$, $qb$They have forgotten what was agreed$qb$, $qb$They want to reopen the whole agreement$qb$, $qb$They are trying to run down the clock$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want a supplier to deliver faster. They say it would cost more. What is the most useful thing to establish?$qb$, $qb$Which parts of the order you actually need first$qb$, $qb$How much faster delivery would cost$qb$, $qb$Whether another supplier is quicker$qb$, $qb$Why their normal delivery takes as long as it does$qb$, $qb$Whether they would do it faster as a favour$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An agreement you reached last year is up for renewal and the other side wants better terms. What is the best preparation?$qb$, $qb$Work out what the agreement is now worth to each side$qb$, $qb$Work out what your minimum acceptable terms are$qb$, $qb$Find out what alternatives are available to you$qb$, $qb$Review what went well and badly over the year$qb$, $qb$Decide how much movement you are willing to offer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to accept a deal today or lose it. You are not ready to decide. What should you establish first?$qb$, $qb$Whether the deadline is real$qb$, $qb$What you would lose if the offer went$qb$, $qb$Whether a similar offer exists elsewhere$qb$, $qb$What makes them want a decision today$qb$, $qb$How long you would actually need$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a small printing business. A regular customer who gives you about a fifth of your work asks for a ten per cent discount on all future orders. You cannot afford ten per cent. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what has prompted the request before you respond to the figure$qb$, $qb$Offer a smaller discount that you can afford to give$qb$, $qb$Explain what your margins are and why ten per cent is not possible$qb$, $qb$Offer the discount on their largest orders only$qb$, $qb$Agree to it, since losing a fifth of your work would be worse$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are buying equipment. The seller has offered a price and says it is available only until Friday. It is Tuesday and you have not compared it with anything else. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Get one comparison this week, and tell the seller that is what you are doing$qb$, $qb$Ask the seller whether the Friday deadline can be extended$qb$, $qb$Compare it with alternatives and accept losing the offer if needed$qb$, $qb$Take the offer, since a deadline suggests the price is genuine$qb$, $qb$Let it pass, since a pressured deadline is a bad sign$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a team. A member has asked for a pay rise you cannot approve. She is good and you do not want to lose her. You have no budget until the next financial year. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell her the position plainly and agree what happens at the year end$qb$, $qb$Tell her there is no budget and that you will review it later$qb$, $qb$Explain what she would need to do to justify a rise$qb$, $qb$Tell her you will do what you can and see what happens$qb$, $qb$Tell her the answer is no and leave it there$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are agreeing a contract. The other side has sent a version with a clause you did not discuss, which shifts a cost onto you. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what the clause is for before saying whether you accept it$qb$, $qb$Say the clause was not discussed and ask for it to be removed$qb$, $qb$Accept it but ask for something in return elsewhere$qb$, $qb$Sign it, since the cost involved is fairly small$qb$, $qb$Refuse to sign until the clause is taken out$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in sales. A customer wants a feature your product does not have, and says he will buy if you can provide it. Building it would take three months. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask what he needs the feature to do, since something existing may cover it$qb$, $qb$Tell him it would take three months and ask if he can wait$qb$, $qb$Offer to build it if he commits to a large enough order$qb$, $qb$Tell him the product does not have it and cannot be changed$qb$, $qb$Say you will look into it and hope he forgets the request$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a tenant negotiating a lease renewal. The landlord wants a fifteen per cent increase. You have found two similar premises nearby at lower rents, but moving would cost you two months of trading. How do you approach the negotiation?$qb$, $qb$Weigh the moving cost against the increase, then negotiate from that figure$qb$, $qb$Tell the landlord you have found cheaper premises nearby$qb$, $qb$Ask the landlord to justify a fifteen per cent increase$qb$, $qb$Offer to accept a smaller increase over a longer lease$qb$, $qb$Accept the increase, since moving would cost more in lost trade$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are buying from a new supplier. Everything is agreed except payment terms: they want payment in seven days and you normally pay in thirty. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask why seven days matters to them before offering anything$qb$, $qb$Offer to meet in the middle at around two weeks$qb$, $qb$Explain that thirty days is your standard across all suppliers$qb$, $qb$Agree to seven days, since everything else is settled$qb$, $qb$Tell them the deal is off unless they accept thirty days$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a department. Another department wants to borrow one of your staff for a month. You can spare her for two weeks without difficulty. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Offer the two weeks and ask what they would do for the rest$qb$, $qb$Offer two weeks and explain why a month is not possible$qb$, $qb$Ask what they need her for before deciding anything$qb$, $qb$Agree to the month and manage the gap somehow$qb$, $qb$Refuse, since a month would leave your own team short$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are quoting for a job. The customer says your price is too high but will not say what she expected to pay. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Ask what she is comparing it with, so you know what is being priced$qb$, $qb$Ask her what figure she had in mind for the work$qb$, $qb$Break the quote down so she can see what she is paying for$qb$, $qb$Offer a lower price to keep the conversation going$qb$, $qb$Hold the quote and let her come back if she wants to$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are agreeing a delivery date with a customer. He wants it in two weeks; you can do four. He says two weeks is essential because of an event. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what he needs ready for the event, since part may be enough$qb$, $qb$Offer to deliver in four weeks and ask whether that would work$qb$, $qb$Tell him two weeks is not possible and explain why$qb$, $qb$Agree to two weeks and try to find a way to manage it$qb$, $qb$Tell him he will need to find another supplier$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are settling a claim with a customer whose order arrived damaged. He is asking for a full refund plus compensation. The goods were damaged by your carrier. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Agree the refund now and ask what the damage actually cost him$qb$, $qb$Agree the refund now and decline the compensation, explaining why$qb$, $qb$Offer a replacement sent out at once instead of a refund$qb$, $qb$Tell him the carrier caused it and he should claim from them$qb$, $qb$Refuse both until the carrier confirms what happened to the goods$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are negotiating with a colleague over who takes on an unpopular task. Neither of you wants it, and it has to be done by someone this week. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Work out which parts each of you minds least and split it that way$qb$, $qb$Offer to take it if he takes the next one that comes up$qb$, $qb$Suggest tossing a coin so that neither feels singled out$qb$, $qb$Point out that he took the last easy job that came along$qb$, $qb$Take it yourself to avoid the disagreement$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a supplier. Your largest customer has asked you to hold your prices for another year while your own costs have risen eight per cent. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Show what has changed in your costs and propose how to share it$qb$, $qb$Explain that your costs have risen and a price rise is needed$qb$, $qb$Offer to hold prices in exchange for a longer commitment$qb$, $qb$Hold the prices and absorb the cost to keep the customer$qb$, $qb$Tell them the price will rise and they can take it or leave it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-NEG-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are agreeing terms for a piece of freelance work. The client has offered a fee you think is low, but the work would lead to more from them later. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Agree a fee for this job and what happens on the next one$qb$, $qb$Accept the lower fee on the basis of the future work$qb$, $qb$Ask for the fee you want and explain what it covers$qb$, $qb$Accept the fee and raise your rate on the next job$qb$, $qb$Decline, since the fee offered is below what you charge$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
