  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A person who feels pushed will defend a position they had not even ______.$qb$, $qb$chosen$qb$, $qb$explained$qb$, $qb$written$qb$, $qb$announced$qb$, $qb$priced$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Persuading the person everyone else listens to saves persuading the rest of the ______.$qb$, $qb$room$qb$, $qb$argument$qb$, $qb$day$qb$, $qb$topic$qb$, $qb$time$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$An idea presented as the listener's own is more likely to be ______.$qb$, $qb$adopted$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$shortened$qb$, $qb$questioned$qb$, $qb$delayed$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Facts change fewer minds than facts attached to a ______.$qb$, $qb$story$qb$, $qb$warning$qb$, $qb$figure$qb$, $qb$goal$qb$, $qb$deadline$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Raising the objection yourself takes it away from the person about to ______ it.$qb$, $qb$make$qb$, $qb$hear$qb$, $qb$write$qb$, $qb$repeat$qb$, $qb$resolve$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Persuasion that relies on pressure works once and costs the next ______.$qb$, $qb$attempt$qb$, $qb$conversation$qb$, $qb$problem$qb$, $qb$sale$qb$, $qb$result$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Knowing what the other person is measured on tells you which argument will ______ them.$qb$, $qb$influence$qb$, $qb$disturb$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, $qb$question$qb$, $qb$involve$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A long case gives the listener more places to ______.$qb$, $qb$disagree$qb$, $qb$concentrate$qb$, $qb$remember$qb$, $qb$decide$qb$, $qb$reply$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Saying what you want the listener to do prevents agreement without ______.$qb$, $qb$action$qb$, $qb$detail$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, $qb$comment$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Repeating a point louder rarely changes a mind that has already ______ it.$qb$, $qb$rejected$qb$, $qb$written$qb$, $qb$shared$qb$, $qb$reported$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The best moment to ask is usually before a decision has been ______.$qb$, $qb$formed$qb$, $qb$changed$qb$, $qb$challenged$qb$, $qb$found$qb$, $qb$lost$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want your manager to approve a change to how your team works. What is most likely to succeed?$qb$, $qb$Showing what problem the change solves for her$qb$, $qb$Explaining in detail how the new way would work$qb$, $qb$Pointing out how much the team dislikes the current way$qb$, $qb$Asking her to try it for a month and see$qb$, $qb$Describing how another team already works this way$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are trying to convince a group and one person is clearly against you. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would need to be true for them to agree$qb$, $qb$Address their objection before anyone raises it$qb$, $qb$Focus on the people who seem open to it$qb$, $qb$Ask them to hold their view until you have finished$qb$, $qb$Speak to them separately after the meeting$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your proposal has one genuine weakness. What should you do about it?$qb$, $qb$Raise it yourself and say how you would handle it$qb$, $qb$Prepare an answer in case someone asks about it$qb$, $qb$Mention it briefly and move on quickly$qb$, $qb$Leave it out unless someone raises it$qb$, $qb$Present only the parts that are strong$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You need a busy senior person to back your idea. What is most likely to get her attention?$qb$, $qb$What it changes for something she is responsible for$qb$, $qb$How much work has gone into developing it$qb$, $qb$How many people in the team support it$qb$, $qb$How straightforward it would be to put in place$qb$, $qb$How long you have been trying to raise it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A customer is unconvinced by your product. What is usually the most useful next step?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would have to be true for it to suit him$qb$, $qb$Explain the features he may have overlooked$qb$, $qb$Offer him a trial so he can judge for himself$qb$, $qb$Compare it with what the competition offers$qb$, $qb$Reduce the price to make the decision easier$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asking your team to adopt a new process they have not asked for. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$That they can see what it fixes for them$qb$, $qb$That they understand how the process works$qb$, $qb$That they know the decision has been made$qb$, $qb$That the change is introduced gradually$qb$, $qb$That they have a chance to raise objections$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two people must approve your proposal. One cares about cost, the other about risk. How should you present it?$qb$, $qb$Cover both, with the cost case and the risk case set out separately$qb$, $qb$Lead with cost, since that is usually the harder to satisfy$qb$, $qb$Present it once and answer whatever each of them asks$qb$, $qb$Speak to each of them separately with a tailored version$qb$, $qb$Present the strongest overall case and let them weigh it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have made your case and the other person has not said no, but has not agreed either. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Ask what is holding them back$qb$, $qb$Ask them to give you a decision by a date$qb$, $qb$Send them more information to consider$qb$, $qb$Give them time and follow up next week$qb$, $qb$Assume they will agree and proceed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want a colleague in another team to change how they send you information. You have no authority over them. What works best?$qb$, $qb$Show what the current way costs them, not just you$qb$, $qb$Explain how much easier your work would be$qb$, $qb$Ask their manager to raise it with them$qb$, $qb$Ask them politely as a personal favour$qb$, $qb$Point out that they are the only team doing it this way$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An audience seems unconvinced by your figures. What is most likely to help?$qb$, $qb$One concrete example of what the figures mean$qb$, $qb$More detail on where the figures came from$qb$, $qb$A simpler version of the same figures$qb$, $qb$An acknowledgement that figures can mislead$qb$, $qb$A stronger statement of your conclusion$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your idea was rejected six months ago. Circumstances have since changed. How should you raise it again?$qb$, $qb$Lead with what has changed since it was refused$qb$, $qb$Present it as a new idea without the history$qb$, $qb$Send them the original proposal again with the new facts added$qb$, $qb$Ask why it was rejected before raising it again$qb$, $qb$Wait until someone else raises the same problem$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are persuading someone who says they have no time to listen. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask for two minutes and say what you need from them$qb$, $qb$Send it in writing so they can read it later$qb$, $qb$Ask when would be a better time to talk$qb$, $qb$Explain that it will not take long$qb$, $qb$Wait for a moment when they are less busy$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are presenting a case to people who will lose something if it is agreed. What should you do?$qb$, $qb$Name what they lose before you make the case$qb$, $qb$Focus on what the organisation gains overall$qb$, $qb$Acknowledge it if someone raises the point$qb$, $qb$Explain that the change is happening either way$qb$, $qb$Present the benefits and leave the losses aside$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone agrees with you in the meeting but does nothing afterwards. What most likely happened?$qb$, $qb$They agreed with the idea but not to doing anything$qb$, $qb$They changed their mind after the meeting$qb$, $qb$They did not have time to act on it$qb$, $qb$They were agreeing to avoid disagreement$qb$, $qb$They did not understand what was being asked$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are trying to persuade someone who trusts a colleague of yours more than you. What is the best approach?$qb$, $qb$Ask your colleague to put the case with you$qb$, $qb$Make the case yourself and let the argument stand$qb$, $qb$Use the same reasoning your colleague would use$qb$, $qb$Mention that your colleague supports the idea$qb$, $qb$Ask your colleague to raise it instead of you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually makes it easier for someone to agree to a request?$qb$, $qb$Being clear about exactly what you are asking for$qb$, $qb$Explaining fully why the request matters$qb$, $qb$Making the request in person rather than in writing$qb$, $qb$Asking at a time when they are not busy$qb$, $qb$Showing that others have already agreed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to change a long-standing practice. Several people defend it strongly. What is most useful to establish first?$qb$, $qb$What the practice is protecting against$qb$, $qb$How long the practice has been in place$qb$, $qb$Who introduced the practice originally$qb$, $qb$Whether other places do it differently$qb$, $qb$How much the practice currently costs$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A senior person has publicly supported a course of action you think is wrong. What is the best way to raise it?$qb$, $qb$Raise it privately with the new information$qb$, $qb$Raise it publicly so the record is corrected$qb$, $qb$Ask a question that lets them reconsider it$qb$, $qb$Raise it with someone more senior than them$qb$, $qb$Let it go, since the position is already public$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
