  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your written proposal will be read by someone who reads only the first paragraph. What should that paragraph contain?$qb$, $qb$What you want them to decide$qb$, $qb$The problem the proposal addresses$qb$, $qb$A summary of the whole proposal$qb$, $qb$The strongest argument in your case$qb$, $qb$The background to why you are writing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a hospital. You believe a new way of handling discharge paperwork would save an hour a day. Your ward manager is overloaded and has turned down two other suggestions this month. How do you raise it?$qb$, $qb$Show her the hour it saves her ward, and offer to trial it yourself first$qb$, $qb$Explain the new method and ask her to consider it when she has time$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague who has her ear to raise it on your behalf$qb$, $qb$Put it in writing so she can read it when she is less busy$qb$, $qb$Wait until she is less overloaded before raising anything new$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a shop supervisor. You want head office to change a display layout that confuses customers in your branch. You have no authority to change it yourself. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Record what customers actually do, and send that with your suggestion$qb$, $qb$Write to head office explaining why the layout confuses customers$qb$, $qb$Ask other branch supervisors whether they see the same problem$qb$, $qb$Change the display locally and see whether anyone objects$qb$, $qb$Raise it at the next area meeting when there is time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a teacher. You want a parent to agree to extra support sessions for their child. The parent has said before that the child is fine and does not need help. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Show what the child struggles with, and what the sessions would change$qb$, $qb$Explain what the extra sessions involve and how they would help$qb$, $qb$Tell the parent that other children are attending them too$qb$, $qb$Explain that the school recommends it for children at this level$qb$, $qb$Arrange the sessions and inform the parent afterwards$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are an engineer. You think a piece of equipment should be replaced before it fails. Your manager says the budget is committed elsewhere this year. How do you make the case?$qb$, $qb$Show what a failure would cost against what replacement costs$qb$, $qb$Explain the signs that suggest the equipment is near the end$qb$, $qb$Ask whether any of the committed budget could be moved$qb$, $qb$Ask him to consider it in next year's budget instead$qb$, $qb$Accept the answer and raise it again if it fails$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in an office. You want your team to start recording a piece of information that would help you but adds two minutes to each of their jobs. How do you ask?$qb$, $qb$Explain what it prevents for them, and ask them to try it for a month$qb$, $qb$Explain why the information is useful and ask them to record it$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager to make the recording a requirement$qb$, $qb$Ask each person individually as a favour to you$qb$, $qb$Start recording it yourself and ask them if you fall behind$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a nurse. A patient is refusing a treatment the doctor has recommended. He says he does not see the point of it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask what concerns him about it, and answer what he actually raises$qb$, $qb$Explain again what the treatment is for and how it works$qb$, $qb$Tell him the doctor has recommended it for good reason$qb$, $qb$Explain what could happen if he does not have it$qb$, $qb$Note the refusal and tell the doctor he has declined$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a small team. You want to move the weekly meeting to a different day. Two people prefer the current day and three have no strong view. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask the two what the current day gives them, before proposing the change$qb$, $qb$Explain why the new day works better and ask for agreement$qb$, $qb$Put it to the team and go with the majority view$qb$, $qb$Move it and see whether the two raise any real difficulty$qb$, $qb$Leave it as it is, since two people prefer the current day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a purchasing officer. You want to switch to a supplier who is cheaper and more reliable. Your director has a long relationship with the current supplier. How do you raise it?$qb$, $qb$Set out the reliability record and let the comparison speak$qb$, $qb$Explain the savings the new supplier would deliver$qb$, $qb$Suggest trialling the new supplier on part of the order$qb$, $qb$Ask the current supplier to match the new one's terms$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the director's relationship matters more$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a project lead. You need three departments to change a small part of their process. None of them reports to you and all three are busy. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Go to each with what the change does for their own work$qb$, $qb$Send all three the same request explaining what is needed$qb$, $qb$Ask your sponsor to instruct all three departments$qb$, $qb$Start with the department most likely to agree$qb$, $qb$Call all three together and explain the project's needs$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a mechanic. A customer needs a repair that costs more than the car is worth. He is attached to the car and wants it fixed. How do you handle the conversation?$qb$, $qb$Give him the figures and let him decide with them in front of him$qb$, $qb$Tell him the repair costs more than the car is worth$qb$, $qb$Recommend that he does not go ahead with the repair$qb$, $qb$Do the repair, since he has asked for it and it is his choice$qb$, $qb$Suggest he gets a second opinion from another garage$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a charity. You want a local business to sponsor an event. They have declined similar requests from other charities this year. How do you approach them?$qb$, $qb$Find what they are trying to achieve locally, and connect the event to it$qb$, $qb$Explain what the event does and what sponsorship would fund$qb$, $qb$Offer them prominent advertising in return for the sponsorship$qb$, $qb$Ask for a smaller amount than the other charities asked for$qb$, $qb$Approach a different business that has not declined before$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a team member, not a manager. You think the way work is allocated is unfair to two quieter colleagues. Nobody has complained. How do you raise it?$qb$, $qb$Show your manager the pattern in the allocation itself$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager that two colleagues seem to be carrying more$qb$, $qb$Encourage the two colleagues to raise it themselves$qb$, $qb$Raise it as a general question about how work is shared$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since nobody involved has complained about it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a trainer. Half your group think the course is a waste of a day and have said so in the first ten minutes. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make the day worth their time, and adjust what you can$qb$, $qb$Explain what the course covers and why it matters$qb$, $qb$Acknowledge their view and continue with the material$qb$, $qb$Ask them to give it an hour before deciding$qb$, $qb$Tell them attendance is required and carry on$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PIC-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A3-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a sales assistant. A customer has decided on a product that will not do what she has described wanting. She is ready to pay. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell her what it will not do, and show her what would$qb$, $qb$Ask her to describe again what she needs it to do$qb$, $qb$Tell her that product may not suit what she wants$qb$, $qb$Sell it to her, since she has made her own choice$qb$, $qb$Sell it and mention the returns policy at the till$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
